    "title": "Eagles Quarterback Joe Milton III to Make First NFL Start",
    "text": "• Eagles quarterback Joe Milton III will start against the New York Giants on Sunday, November 8, 2026.\n• Milton will be making his first NFL start after joining the Eagles three weeks ago from the Dallas Cowboys' practice squad.\n• The Eagles have lost six consecutive games, and Milton will be taking over a team that has struggled to protect its quarterback, sustain drives, and score points.\n• Milton has a cannon for an arm, good mobility, and the ability to extend plays when protection breaks down.\n• He has limited experience in the Eagles' offense, but has been learning the playbook with the help of quarterbacks coach Parks Frazier and former quarterback Tanner McKee.\n• Milton has a combination of arm strength and athleticism, but questions remain about his accuracy and consistency.\n• He has been preparing for the start by going through the plays and being ready, just like a starter.\n• Milton has a young daughter, and he uses nightly FaceTime conversations with her to maintain perspective and stay thankful.\n• The Eagles' injury report includes several players who are listed as DNP, limited, or full participants in practice.",
    "summary": "The 26-year-old quarterback will make his first NFL start Sunday against the New York Giants, taking over a team that has lost six consecutive games. Milton, who joined the Eagles just three weeks ago from the Dallas Cowboys’ practice squad, sounded ready Thursday. Milton said Mannion’s West Coast system resembles the offense he learned as a rookie in New England under Alex Van Pelt. He subsequently played four games for Dallas in 2025 before the Eagles signed him off the Cowboys’ practice squad Oct. 16 following Jalen Hurts’ blood-clot diagnosis.",
